# Every five minutes, all day.
#
# The session gate lives in the command rather than here, because a timer
# has no idea what a trading session is and a calendar in two places is a
# calendar that will disagree with itself. Out of hours the pass reads the
# calendar, logs that every market is closed, and exits -- which costs a
# second and keeps the schedule honest about what it is.
#
# Five minutes rather than the analysis's cadence on purpose. Closing is the
# time-critical half: a position that should be shut wants shutting now, not
# when the next pipeline happens to finish. Opening is rate-limited by the
# signal itself -- the engine only changes its mind when a bar completes --
# so a faster dealer cannot overtrade, it can only react sooner.
#
# Persistent=false, deliberately. A missed dealing pass is not worth catching
# up on after a reboot: the decision it would have acted on is stale by then,
# and `decision_is_stale` would refuse the opens anyway. Firing a backlog of
# them at boot would be noise at best.

[Unit]
Description=Deal on the Capital demo account every 5 minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=3min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min
AccuracySec=15s
Persistent=false

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
